coverage:
I read all of Sections 0, 1, 3, 7 and 8. In Section 2 I read the statements and proof outlines (strata, perfection, the Kummer stalk bound, summed Ext, bounded tiltings, projective images, the projected-norm lemma and the final proof). In Sections 5 and 6 I read most of the text: runner localization, ordered swaps, type-D folding, the cohook d=1 and d=2 moves, the condition-number and cone-transfer lemmas, the triangle endpoint, the residual and linear cuspidal modules, inertia, heads, Hecke presentation, extension, parameters, the even-subalgebra count, exhaustion and the final norm bound. In Section 4 I read the Fourier separation, minimum-norm and single-cycle transport lemmas.

Checks performed by hand:
- the regular-datum lattice glue table and its diagram compatibility (types B, C, D, both parities of n);
- the hook/cohook count H = 2n - floor(u/2) + c;
- the type A LTE inequality chain and the torus-centralizer case;
- the p=2 centrality argument;
- the cone-volume formula;
- the d=2 rotation-coefficient count;
- the telescoping identity R_d(x) * prod_a R_p(x^{d p^a}) = P(x), which makes the Hecke simple-type count equal |T|.

Also checked: the Lang-theorem descent in based Sylow descent; the H^2 restriction-finiteness and torsor argument in the kernel-removal lemma; the scalar-cocycle removal; the twist bookkeeping lambda_m and sigma^m(b_L) = lambda_m b_L in Lemma per:row-return; and the coefficient extension to K. I did not verify the deep sheaf-theoretic details of Section 2, and I did not check the contents of the cited theorems (EEL, Eisele, Bonnafe-Rouquier, Cabanes-Enguehard, Du-Rui) against their sources.
